(1209, 309, 'Use statistics as measures of centre and spread of a data distribution, being aware of their limitations.', 8),
(1210, 311, 'Construct and use parallel box plots, including identifying possible outliers, to compare datasets in terms of median, spread (range and IQR) and outliers to interpret and communicate the differences observed in the context of the data.; outliers (identifying): $Q_{1} - 1.5 \times \text{IQR} \le x \le Q_{3} + 1.5 \times \text{IQR}$ where $Q_{1}$ is lower quartile and $Q_{3}$ is upper quartile', 0),
