(1223, 316, 'Understand and use $m = r\frac{s_{y}}{s_{x}}$ and $c = \bar{y} - m\bar{x}$ to determine the equation of a least-squares line, where $m$ is slope (gradient), $r$ is correlation coefficient, $s_{y}$ is (sample) standard deviation of $y$ values, $s_{x}$ is (sample) standard deviation of $x$ values, $c$ is $y$-intercept, $\bar{y}$ is mean of $y$ values and $\bar{x}$ is mean of $x$ values.', 1),
