(1245, 323, 'Use geometric sequences to model and analyse practical situations involving geometric growth and decay (use of logarithms not required), e.g. modelling the growth of a bacterial population that doubles in size each hour, calculating the value of an item using the diminishing-value method of depreciation.', 3),
