(1556, 422, 'Prove and apply the angle sum, difference and double-angle identities for sines and cosines.; $\sin(A + B) = \sin(A)\cos(B) + \cos(A)\sin(B)$; $\sin(A - B) = \sin(A)\cos(B) - \cos(A)\sin(B)$; $\cos(A + B) = \cos(A)\cos(B) - \sin(A)\sin(B)$; $\cos(A - B) = \cos(A)\cos(B) + \sin(A)\sin(B)$; $\sin(2A) = 2\sin(A)\cos(A)$; $\cos(2A) = \cos^{2}(A) - \sin^{2}(A) = 1 - 2\sin^{2}(A) = 2\cos^{2}(A) - 1$', 1),
(1557, 422, 'Prove and apply the identities for products of sines and cosines expressed as sums and differences.; $\sin(A)\sin(B) = \frac{1}{2}(\cos(A - B) - \cos(A + B))$; $\cos(A)\cos(B) = \frac{1}{2}(\cos(A - B) + \cos(A + B))$; $\sin(A)\cos(B) = \frac{1}{2}(\sin(A + B) + \sin(A - B))$; $\cos(A)\sin(B) = \frac{1}{2}(\sin(A + B) - \sin(A - B))$', 2),
